ns (summary + description/priority/status/assignee in one allowlisted dict): whether the executor route is entered only for summary-exclusive field sets or peels summary out of a larger dict.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["dispatch_one.py:621: `result = _call_with_retry(client.update_issue, issue_key, **_extra, **fields)` forwards the entire allowlisted field dict, not a summary-only kwarg","Plan step 3: 'Route summary-only updates to the executor instead of _call_with_retry(client.update_issue, ...)' and 'The summary-family flag defaults to the executor'","_update_one_scalar_update also carries description/priority/status/assignee per _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST, so a real mutation frequently combines summary with other fields"],"finding":"The plan names dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update as the summary route edit target, but that function forwards the WHOLE allowlisted field dict (summary, description, priority, status, assignee) as client.update_issue(key, **fields); the plan routes only 'summary-only updates' to the executor and leaves unspecified how mixed-field mutations (summary + other fields arriving in the same allowlisted dict) are classified — whether they stay on _call_with_retry or split.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbbc8ced6e2ed3346","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3; dispatch_one.py:621 (_update_one_scalar_update)","norm_id":"nbbc4e65441d45571","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reconcile pass that changes both summary and description on one issue reaches _update_one_scalar_update with a two-key field dict","Reviewer/implementer cannot tell whether such a mixed mutation takes the new executor budget or the legacy _call_with_retry wrapper"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_